  "description": "<p>Verifying an export that used application/ld+json format caused</p>\n\n<p>Running verification on Fedora 4 export<br/>\nTraceback (most recent call last):<br/>\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.5/site-packages/rdflib/plugin.py\", line 100, in get<br/>\n    p = _plugins<span class=\"error\">&#91;(name, kind)&#93;</span><br/>\nKeyError: ('application/ld+json', &lt;class 'rdflib.parser.Parser'&gt;)</p>\n\n<p>During handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:</p>\n\n<p>Traceback (most recent call last):<br/>\n  File \"./verify.py\", line 457, in &lt;module&gt;<br/>\n    main()<br/>\n  File \"./verify.py\", line 378, in main<br/>\n    destination = Resource(original.destpath, config, logger)<br/>\n  File \"./verify.py\", line 261, in _<em>init</em>_<br/>\n    format=config.lang<br/>\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.5/site-packages/rdflib/graph.py\", line 1040, in parse<br/>\n    parser = plugin.get(format, Parser)()<br/>\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.5/site-packages/rdflib/plugin.py\", line 103, in get<br/>\n    \"No plugin registered for (%s, %s)\" % (name, kind))<br/>\nrdflib.plugin.PluginException: No plugin registered for (application/ld+json, &lt;class 'rdflib.parser.Parser'&gt;)</p>\n\n<p>Need to install rdflib-jsonld to support that language.</p>",
